<!--
  FreeCash-Daily-Monitor-R4.xml · stream S5 (scheduler) · delegation R4 · 2026-10-01

  STATUS: PROPOSAL ONLY. This file registers NOTHING. No task whose name contains
  "FreeCash" exists on this host (verified live this pass; raw/02, raw/03). A
  scheduled task that does not exist cannot fire, so this XML is inert until a
  human registers it.

  RULE NUMBERING (operator numbering, authoritative in this delegation):
    R1 NO EARNING ACTION · R2 ONCE PER DAY · R3 NOTIFY ON CHANGE ·
    R4 APPROVAL BEFORE EXTERNAL ACTION
  Registering a task is an external, state-changing action, so rule
  R4 APPROVAL BEFORE EXTERNAL ACTION withholds registration until the operator
  approves in writing. The approval command is printed in SCHEDULER-DECISION.md
  section 6 and must be run by the operator, never by an agent.

  Titles are printed next to every rule reference on purpose. The shipped code
  inverts R1 and R2 in its own docstrings (gate.py:1 calls once-per-day "R1";
  readonly_client.py:1 calls the read-only network path "R2"), so a reader who
  takes a bare R-number from either source will mis-map the rule.

  INTERPRETER, PINNED
    C:\Users\cd-pr\AppData\Local\hermes\hermes-agent\venv\Scripts\python.exe
  Re-verified this pass: that interpreter reports 3.11.9 and resolves
  ZoneInfo("Europe/Berlin"). Both py -3.11 and py -3.14 raise
  ZoneInfoNotFoundError for the same key. gate.resolve_tz() fails open to the
  machine zone and reports kind "system-local", so a scheduler pointed at the
  wrong interpreter would not crash: it would silently move the operator-local
  day key and quietly break R2 ONCE PER DAY. Never change this path to python3,
  py or pythonw.

  OBSERVE-ONLY ACTION
  The task runs exactly one script, D:\AgenticOS\monitoring\freecash\run_daily_check.py,
  with exactly one flag, the read source pin (source=operator_state). No second
  command, no chained shell operator, no write verb, no approval execution, no
  earning path. That property is asserted mechanically by xml_gate.py, which was
  shown to reject twelve planted mutants (raw/17) and to accept this file (raw/18).

  NO WRAPPER, AND WHAT IT COSTS
  schtasks cannot set environment variables. The routine's production values are
  its own code defaults (paths.py:35 DEFAULT_DATA_ROOT, gate.py DEFAULT_TZ,
  run_daily_check.py:52 DEFAULT_SOURCE), so a service-spawned task's environment
  is deterministic. A .cmd wrapper that exported FREECASH_DATA_ROOT would point
  production at a throwaway root, which is the opposite of what production
  needs, so no wrapper is used. The cost: stdout has to be redirected from the
  Arguments string, which is why the redirect lives there. No path in this file
  contains a space, so the unquoted cmd.exe form is used; that exact form was
  executed end to end this pass through cmd.exe (raw/14).

  START BOUNDARY, AND THE CATCH-UP BURN
  StartBoundary is 2026-10-05T09:00:00 (a Monday), deliberately in the future.
  With StartWhenAvailable=true, registering a task whose StartBoundary is
  already in the past fires ONE catch-up run at registration time. Because
  run_daily_check.py acquires the day lock at :309 BEFORE it reads the source at
  :372, that catch-up run consumes the day while reading nothing, and the lock
  is never cleared, so that day can never carry a reading. raw/14 reproduces
  exactly that outcome on a throwaway root:
      RUN_OK 2026-10-01 outcome=MONITOR_DEGRADED
      source=operator_entered(data_available=False)
      snapshot=2026-10-01.json written=True changes=0 notifications=0
  If the operator registers this file after 2026-10-05T09:00 local, MOVE THE
  START BOUNDARY FORWARD FIRST or that day is burnt. This is a property of the
  entry point, not of the schedule; the durable fix is the pre-flight wrapper
  owned by stream S1 (workflow/), which should refuse to invoke the entry point
  on a day whose source record is absent.

  NO RESTART ON FAILURE, DELIBERATELY
  run_daily_check.py's exit table gives 5 for "the status read failed; the day
  lock stays in place, no automatic re-run". A retry inside the same day can
  only print SKIP_DUPLICATE_DAY, so a RestartOnFailure element would add noise
  and no coverage. There is none.

  NO SECRETS. The routine holds no credential, token, cookie or password, and
  this file contains none. Its read-only transport is allowlisted to loopback.
-->
